WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.633 --> 00:00:03.403
[waves crashing]

00:00:12.812 --> 00:00:15.815
[helicopter sounds]

00:00:26.226 --> 00:00:28.928
You have to be pretty top
notch in your profession

00:00:28.995 --> 00:00:30.263
just to survive it all.

00:00:33.967 --> 00:00:35.301
You get heavy turbulence.

00:00:35.368 --> 00:00:36.736
You've got to slow
the aircraft down,

00:00:36.803 --> 00:00:39.005
because you could have
structural failure.

00:00:39.072 --> 00:00:42.675
Losing a wing
wouldn't be much fun.

00:00:42.742 --> 00:00:45.178
A North Atlantic
storm in November.

00:00:45.245 --> 00:00:49.382
It's a pretty impressive
event, to put it mildly.

00:00:49.449 --> 00:00:51.684
My name is John
Raymond Boulanger.

00:00:51.751 --> 00:00:55.555
I'm what you would
call a mercenary pilot.

00:00:55.622 --> 00:00:59.826
I fly for hire to he
who pays the most.

00:01:03.997 --> 00:01:11.037
I had 4,343 kilos of cocaine,
and I was flying from Colombia

00:01:11.104 --> 00:01:12.739
directly to Canada.

00:01:12.806 --> 00:01:16.943
Normally, the flight would be
about nine hours, give or take.

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:20.713
But I ran into this storm for
about 45 minutes or an hour

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:22.248
before I broke out.

00:01:22.315 --> 00:01:24.284
And, lo and behold,
there were the FATs.

00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:27.320
[jet engine sounds]

00:01:28.154 --> 00:01:29.522
Then they were off to my rear.

00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:39.132
And the other guy came up close
beside us and flying around me,

00:01:39.199 --> 00:01:40.800
making signals to go down.

00:01:40.867 --> 00:01:42.001
I just waved to them.

00:01:42.068 --> 00:01:44.404
They can't shoot at you.

00:01:44.471 --> 00:01:46.673
But they were
running out of gas.

00:01:46.739 --> 00:01:48.208
We would just time
the guy and say,

00:01:48.274 --> 00:01:50.109
OK, how long is it going
to be before they're

00:01:50.176 --> 00:01:51.277
going to run out?

00:01:56.015 --> 00:01:57.283
It was interesting.

00:01:57.350 --> 00:01:58.751
He gave us a nice little show.

00:02:03.089 --> 00:02:05.124
I went down to treetop level.

00:02:05.191 --> 00:02:09.395
I flew the rest of
the way treetop level,

00:02:09.462 --> 00:02:11.798
below radar so nobody knew
where the airplane was.

00:02:14.367 --> 00:02:17.470
The authorities put out an
alert to all the airports.

00:02:17.537 --> 00:02:20.240
There's a big white Convair
somewhere in Canada,

00:02:20.306 --> 00:02:22.909
if anybody sought to report it.

00:02:22.976 --> 00:02:25.612
I should have arrived around
6 o'clock in the morning

00:02:25.678 --> 00:02:27.847
but I arrived at
quarter to nine instead.

00:02:32.652 --> 00:02:34.287
I was standing
out on the runway,

00:02:34.354 --> 00:02:36.890
waiting for the crew hired
to go and do the pick up.

00:02:40.460 --> 00:02:42.428
We looked all over the
place, couldn't figure out

00:02:42.495 --> 00:02:44.364
where the hell these guys were.

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:46.900
Turns out they had been there
since 3:00 in the morning.

00:02:46.966 --> 00:02:50.303
At around 7:30, they decided I
wasn't coming, and they left.

00:02:52.772 --> 00:02:54.841
So anyway, I started
walking, and a truck went by.

00:02:54.908 --> 00:02:57.710
I hitchhiked, and he gave
me a lift all the way down

00:02:57.777 --> 00:02:59.479
to the lumber camp.

00:02:59.546 --> 00:03:01.881
And that's where I was
when the RCMP arrived

00:03:01.948 --> 00:03:03.182
by helicopter,
because the police

00:03:03.249 --> 00:03:04.651
had blocked off all the roads.

00:03:06.586 --> 00:03:08.187
So they asked, what's
in the airplane?

00:03:08.254 --> 00:03:08.955
I said, "Cocaine."

00:03:09.022 --> 00:03:09.856
He says, how much?

00:03:09.923 --> 00:03:11.124
I says, "A lot."

00:03:11.190 --> 00:03:12.692
It's being touted
as the biggest

00:03:12.759 --> 00:03:16.162
drug bust in Canadian history
and probably the most dramatic.

00:03:16.229 --> 00:03:18.865
[suspenseful music]

00:03:20.600 --> 00:03:24.270
CHRIS FEISTL: The seizure of
4,300 kilos of cocaine really

00:03:24.337 --> 00:03:25.872
reverberated through DEA.

00:03:28.908 --> 00:03:32.378
That's a staggering amount of
cocaine, coupled with the fact

00:03:32.445 --> 00:03:35.548
that it was flown directly from
the north coast of Colombia

00:03:35.615 --> 00:03:36.516
into Canada.

00:03:52.398 --> 00:03:56.536
JOHN RAYMOND BOULANGER: I would
have made around 45 million.

00:03:56.603 --> 00:03:59.639
It's a pretty good payday
for one day's work.

00:03:59.706 --> 00:04:00.573
That's not bad.

00:04:03.910 --> 00:04:10.049
I was arrested, pled
guilty, and got 23 years.

00:04:10.116 --> 00:04:13.186
That was it, and
I became famous.

00:04:13.252 --> 00:04:18.758
But I take things with
a grain of salt. It was,

00:04:18.825 --> 00:04:22.662
and I believe it still is, the
biggest bust ever in Canada.

